  "aiContextParagraph": "The political landscape in Uttar Pradesh is currently defined by seat-sharing negotiations between the Samajwadi Party and Congress ahead of the 2027 assembly elections. These talks, aimed at consolidating electoral strength, have involved discussions on seat allocation and political strategy. While Congress reportedly proposed a plan involving 130 seats, the Samajwadi Party has presented a revised offer of 26 seats, citing concerns regarding electoral risk and winnability. The process remains active as representatives meet in Delhi to finalize the arrangement. Meanwhile, other political entities, including the Bharatiya Janata Party, have expressed confidence in their electoral standing, focusing on winnable candidates while navigating their own alliance dynamics. The outcome of these discussions is viewed as critical for opposition strategy in the state, with ongoing friction influencing the overall electoral discourse and partnership viability among the involved political parties.",
